{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7d1f3a2-6c54-4f0b-9a21-3d5e7c9f1a80",
    "name": "paynad — payment platform",
    "description": "Every endpoint of the three services, plus a chained scenario that runs a payment from an empty database to a settled ledger.\n\nSelect the **paynad — local** environment first. The stack must be up and migrated: `make up && make migrate && make seed`.\n\nEvery request carries `x-correlation-id`, so one run is one grep across all three services: `docker compose logs | grep $(correlation_id)`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Scenario — one payment, end to end",
      "description": "Run this folder with the collection runner. Every reference is captured by the request that produced it, so nothing is copied by hand: a user, two wallets, a settled payment, its replay, the ledger catching up, and a payment the balance cannot cover.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Create a user",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accounts_url}}/users",
              "host": [
                "{{accounts_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"customer_firstname\": \"Awa\",\n  \"customer_lastname\": \"Traoré\",\n  \"customer_email\": \"scenario-{{run_id}}@example.com\",\n  \"customer_phone_number\": \"+2250700000011\",\n  \"customer_city\": \"Abidjan\",\n  \"customer_country\": \"CI\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// One run id ties every fixture and every log line together.",
                  "pm.environment.set('run_id', Date.now().toString());",
                  "pm.environment.set('correlation_id', 'postman-' + Date.now());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const envelope = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('the envelope is well formed', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(envelope).to.have.all.keys('code', 'message', 'data');",
                  "  pm.expect(envelope.code).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('the user is created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const user = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.expect(user.reference).to.match(/^usr_/);",
                  "pm.environment.set('user_reference', user.reference);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Open the source wallet (500 000)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accounts_url}}/accounts",
              "host": [
                "{{accounts_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "accounts"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_reference\": \"{{user_reference}}\",\n  \"currency\": \"XOF\",\n  \"initial_balance\": 500000,\n  \"label\": \"Scenario source {{run_id}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('the wallet is opened', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const wallet = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.expect(wallet.balance).to.eql(500000);",
                  "pm.environment.set('source_wallet_reference', wallet.reference);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Open the destination wallet (empty)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accounts_url}}/accounts",
              "host": [
                "{{accounts_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "accounts"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_reference\": \"{{user_reference}}\",\n  \"currency\": \"XOF\",\n  \"initial_balance\": 0,\n  \"label\": \"Scenario destination {{run_id}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const wallet = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.expect(wallet.balance).to.eql(0);",
                  "pm.environment.set('destination_wallet_reference', wallet.reference);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Pay 15 000 from source to destination",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{payments_url}}/payments",
              "host": [
                "{{payments_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "payments"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"transaction_id\": \"scenario-{{run_id}}\",\n  \"source_wallet_reference\": \"{{source_wallet_reference}}\",\n  \"destination_wallet_reference\": \"{{destination_wallet_reference}}\",\n  \"amount\": 15000,\n  \"currency\": \"XOF\",\n  \"description\": \"Paiement facture avril\",\n  \"lang\": \"fr\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"user_reference\": \"{{user_reference}}\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('the payment is created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const payment = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('it settled', () => pm.expect(payment.status).to.eql('Approved'));",
                  "pm.test('both legs are recorded', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(payment.debit_transaction_reference).to.match(/^trx_/);",
                  "  pm.expect(payment.credit_transaction_reference).to.match(/^trx_/);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.expect(payment.failure_reason).to.eql(null);",
                  "pm.environment.set('payment_reference', payment.reference);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Replay the same transaction_id",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{payments_url}}/payments",
              "host": [
                "{{payments_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "payments"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"transaction_id\": \"scenario-{{run_id}}\",\n  \"source_wallet_reference\": \"{{source_wallet_reference}}\",\n  \"destination_wallet_reference\": \"{{destination_wallet_reference}}\",\n  \"amount\": 15000,\n  \"currency\": \"XOF\",\n  \"description\": \"Paiement facture avril\",\n  \"lang\": \"fr\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"user_reference\": \"{{user_reference}}\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Same key, same body: the stored response comes back and no money moves."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const payment = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('the very same payment is returned', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(payment.reference).to.eql(pm.environment.get('payment_reference')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Replay it with a different amount → 409",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{payments_url}}/payments",
              "host": [
                "{{payments_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "payments"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"transaction_id\": \"scenario-{{run_id}}\",\n  \"source_wallet_reference\": \"{{source_wallet_reference}}\",\n  \"destination_wallet_reference\": \"{{destination_wallet_reference}}\",\n  \"amount\": 9000,\n  \"currency\": \"XOF\",\n  \"description\": \"Paiement facture avril\",\n  \"lang\": \"fr\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"user_reference\": \"{{user_reference}}\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('the caller contradicting itself is a 409', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "7. The money moved exactly once — source",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accounts_url}}/accounts/{{source_wallet_reference}}/balance",
              "host": [
                "{{accounts_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "accounts",
                "{{source_wallet_reference}}",
                "balance"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('the source is down 15 000', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.balance).to.eql(485000));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "8. The money moved exactly once — destination",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accounts_url}}/accounts/{{destination_wallet_reference}}/balance",
              "host": [
                "{{accounts_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "accounts",
                "{{destination_wallet_reference}}",
                "balance"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('the destination is up 15 000', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.balance).to.eql(15000));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "9. The ledger catches up",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{transactions_url}}/transactions?wallet_reference={{source_wallet_reference}}&per_page=20",
              "host": [
                "{{transactions_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "transactions"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "wallet_reference",
                  "value": "{{source_wallet_reference}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "per_page",
                  "value": "20"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "The ledger is fed through the outbox and the broker, so it is eventually consistent. This request waits, then retries itself a few times rather than asserting on a race it would lose."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// The relay drains every two seconds; give it one pass before looking.",
                  "setTimeout(() => {}, 2500);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const items = pm.response.json().data.items;",
                  "const debit = items.find((line) =>",
                  "  line.payment_reference === pm.environment.get('payment_reference') && line.type === 'DEBIT');",
                  "const attempts = Number(pm.environment.get('ledger_attempts') || 0);",
                  "if (!debit && attempts < 5) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('ledger_attempts', attempts + 1);",
                  "  postman.setNextRequest('9. The ledger catches up');",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('ledger_attempts');",
                  "  pm.test('the debit reached the ledger', () => pm.expect(debit).to.not.be.undefined);",
                  "  pm.test('it is journalised as a DEBIT of 15 000', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(debit.type).to.eql('DEBIT');",
                  "    pm.expect(debit.amount).to.eql(15000);",
                  "  });",
                  "  pm.environment.set('transaction_reference', debit.reference);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "10. A payment the balance cannot cover",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{payments_url}}/payments",
              "host": [
                "{{payments_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "payments"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"transaction_id\": \"scenario-{{run_id}}-short\",\n  \"source_wallet_reference\": \"{{destination_wallet_reference}}\",\n  \"destination_wallet_reference\": \"{{source_wallet_reference}}\",\n  \"amount\": 1000000,\n  \"currency\": \"XOF\",\n  \"description\": \"Paiement trop grand\",\n  \"lang\": \"fr\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"user_reference\": \"{{user_reference}}\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "A refusal is still a payment: 201 with status Declined, so the caller keeps a reference to reconcile with. Nothing moved and nothing is journalised."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('a refusal is still a resource', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const payment = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('it is declined, not errored', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(payment.status).to.eql('Declined');",
                  "  pm.expect(payment.failure_reason).to.eql('INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE');",
                  "  pm.expect(payment.debit_transaction_reference).to.eql(null);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "11. Read the settled payment back",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-correlation-id",
                "value": "{{correlation_id}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{payments_url}}/payments/{{payment_reference}}",
              "host": [
                "{{payments_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "payments",
                "{{payment_reference}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('the projection agrees with the command', () => {",
                  "  const payment = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "  pm.expect(payment.reference).to.eql(pm.environment.get('payment_reference'));",
                  "  pm.expect(payment.status).to.eql('Approved');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
